From: pgf@srl02.cacs.usl.edu (Phil G. Fraering)
Date: Thu, 15 Sep 1994 18:22:09 -0500
Subject: [#94-9-152] Forward: SETIQuest Magazine - A New Publication

One criticism I've seen of the Drake scenario is that any
civilization with the power to spare to do that sort of
communication program would also probably be doing space
colonization to the point where interstellar travel would
be trivial, thus putting us back to the Fermi Paradox.

The researcher that gave a lecture on this scenario at USL
did so in much more detail than I've given here; in the 
question and answer period, some of the professors here
asked about whether they should be looking for infrared
excesses, and where would these be around target stars.

Apparently the infrared excess around Beta Pictoris is in
roughly the right place, if most of the possible civilization's
industry is based around the refining of plastics.

Phil Fraering
