Comic books have some extropian memes, but as far as transhumanism
goes, they are usually entropic in the extreme.

Superheroes often go for low level transformation, like reading,
exercise, diet, etc. I can't recall transhumanist transformations even
attempted by a superhero. Few gained their powers through conscious
self transformation; the vast majority gained their powers by birth or
freak accident.

By contrast, quite a lot of the bad guys are transhumanist. A lot of
the extended stories are about some evil one trying to attain godhood. 	

I can think of some good guys who gained powers through gadgets, but
no transhumanist superhero comes to mind. I suppose that given the
thousands of comics out there, there must be a few, but on the whole,
serious transhumanism comes across as evil in the comic book world.

