  A good example of this is X-Men, particularly, the phoenix saga
which aired last week.  The X-men encounter extraterrestials
for the first time. Their powers are far superior to those of the
x-men (they simply can't compete), however, Jean Grey is accidentally
enveloped by an energy contrail from a crystal which the aliens
are fighting over. That energy transforms her into Phoenix, a being
capable of laying waste to entire planets. The bad guy, who is
trying to get the crystal, finally obtains it and starts the
transformation of the galaxy into "a living galaxy" He will cause
the death of a billion worlds in the process. It turns out,
what the crystal does is change the entire galaxyinto a superbrain
and uploads the user into it. In the final battle, the x-men
(and the powerful extrarterrestials) are no match for the "blight"
who rearranges matter at will. So Phoenix (who was struck down
earlier), rises once more and finds a way to stop the crystal
sealing this bad guy in his own little baby universe (she stopped
the transformation of the galaxy before it d been fully converted)
She then grabs the crystal and flies it into the heart of a star
"where no living being could possibly get ahold of it again"
She must remain with the crystal to guard it because it can't
be destroyed. (this is a cop-out. In the original comic book, Jean/Phoenix
is killed. However, TV standards don't permit cartoons to kill
people, so she leaves the x-men forever trapped in a star to protect
the crystal for eternity)

The X-men all got their powers through genetic mutation.

Wolverine: his power is technically possible. He has an all metal
skeleton inside his flesh, super fast healing ability, better senses,
and metalic claws extend from his knuckles.

Storm: control of the weather. Kinda hard to do.

Cyclops: force beams emanate from eyes. (they are not lasers, they do
not cut/heat. They literally repel/push things)

Beast: ape looking muscular guy with great agility. Genetic engineering?

Rogue: like superman, but she has to power to absorb the powers
of other mutants

Gambit: like King Midas, everything he touches -- turns into an
explosive. (nanotech conversion of local surface into C4 explosive?)

Jubilee: bright lights emanate from her hands. She can blind
people (and the beams sorta push people back) 

There are plenty of other x-men. It should be noted that Wolverine
got his powers because an evil scientist kidnapped him
and experimented on him (to create the ultimate soldier)


